IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `wiv-dates`
IMPORT `wiv-rules`
IMPORT `wiv-seat`

-- Workforce Inspectorate Victoria Act 2020 (Vic) -- worked cases for the worker's questions (wiv-seat.l4), the date
-- helpers (wiv-dates.l4) and the shared rules (wiv-rules.l4). Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited
-- text; none was copied from the encoding's output. Each assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not
-- about the law. The facts are illustrative.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases`

`d` MEANS `the calendar date`
`any day` MEANS `d` 1 1 2000

-- Short names for the answers and choices.
`repealed` MEANS `it does not arise: repealed by the Wage Theft Amendment Act 2025 (No. 35/2025) from 12 December 2025`
`in force then` MEANS `not answered here: in force on that day, but repealed by the Wage Theft Amendment Act 2025 (No. 35/2025) from 12 December 2025, and its text is not in the deposited version`
`not yet` MEANS `it does not arise: the Wage Theft Act 2020 was not yet in operation (it came into operation on 1 July 2021, s 2(2))`

`Part 2` MEANS `Part 2 -- the wage theft offences (ss 6 to 18)`
`Part 4` MEANS `Part 4 -- inspectors and their powers (ss 32 to 62)`
`Div 1` MEANS `Part 5 Division 1 (ss 63 to 65)`
`Div 3` MEANS `Part 5 Division 3 (the former ss 71 to 73)`

`paid` MEANS `employed on a paid basis`
`volunteer` MEANS `employed on a voluntary basis`
`contractor` MEANS `engaged as an independent contractor`
`no engagement` MEANS `engaged in none of these ways`
`site` MEANS `at or in relation to a workplace that is not residential premises`
`residence` MEANS `at or in relation to residential premises where work is carried out, outside any part that is someone's domestic home`
`home only` MEANS `only in a part of premises that is someone's domestic home`
`no workplace` MEANS `not at or in relation to any workplace`

`necessary` MEANS `reasonably necessary for the person to perform their functions or exercise their powers under this Act`
`ib or id` MEANS `in accordance with the Inspectorate's functions under s 20(1)(ib) or (id) (referring public construction matters, advising the Minister)`
`court` MEANS `to a court or VCAT in the course of legal proceedings`
`order` MEANS `under an order of a court or VCAT`
`enforcement` MEANS `to the extent reasonably required to enable the investigation or enforcement of a law of Victoria, another State or Territory or the Commonwealth`
`consent` MEANS `with the written consent of the person to whom the information relates`
`by law` MEANS `required by law`
`no reason` MEANS `none of the s 77(2) circumstances`

`no duty` MEANS `the Act puts no duty on the agency on these facts`
`no time` MEANS `the Inspectorate specified no time: the Act says only within a reasonable time`
`in time` MEANS `provided in time`
`late` MEANS `not provided in time`
`running` MEANS `the time to provide it is still running`

`ib` MEANS `referring public construction complaints or matters, and disclosing related information, to other agencies (s 20(1)(ib))`
`staff` MEANS `employing or engaging employees, consultants or others (s 23(1), (2), (3))`
`other function` MEANS `another function of the Inspectorate`

`the Inspectorate answers` MEANS `the Workforce Inspectorate Victoria answers for it, not the person personally (s 75)`
`s 75 silent` MEANS `s 75 does not apply on these facts: the Act does not say who answers for it`

`harassment` MEANS `intimidation or harassment`
`adverse treatment` MEANS `discrimination, disadvantage or adverse treatment in or in connection with employment`
`dismissal` MEANS `dismissal from, or prejudice in or in connection with, employment`
`discipline` MEANS `disciplinary proceedings in or in connection with employment`
`done` MEANS `it was done to me`
`threatened` MEANS `it was threatened`
`complained` MEANS `I had made a complaint to the Inspectorate`
`gave info` MEANS `I had provided information about public construction to the Inspectorate`
`considering` MEANS `I intended to make, or was considering whether to make, a complaint to the Inspectorate`
`may give info` MEANS `I intended to provide, or was considering whether to provide, information about public construction to the Inspectorate`
`took part` MEANS `I had participated, or was participating, in a process arising from a complaint to the Inspectorate`
`may take part` MEANS `I intended to participate, or was considering whether to participate, in such a process`
`nothing known` MEANS `none of the s 69A(1) matters`

`s 69A` MEANS `s 69A -- causing or threatening detriment because of a complaint to the Inspectorate`
`s 70(1)` MEANS `s 70(1) -- giving information to the Inspectorate believed false or misleading`
`s 70(2)` MEANS `s 70(2) -- producing a document to the Inspectorate known to be false or misleading`
`s 77(1)` MEANS `s 77(1) -- disclosing information obtained under this Act without authority`

§§ `Dates`

#ASSERT `the date` 14 `days after` (`d` 5 1 2026) EQUALS `d` 19 1 2026
#ASSERT `the date` 14 `days after` (`d` 15 2 2028) EQUALS `d` 29 2 2028
#ASSERT `the days from` (`d` 17 12 2025) `to` (`d` 1 1 2026) EQUALS 15
#ASSERT (`d` 12 12 2025) `is on or after` `the day of the 2025 repeals and the name change`
#ASSERT (`d` 11 12 2025) `is before` `the day of the 2025 repeals and the name change`

§§ `The repealed provisions`

