-- A worker underpaid in January 2026: the wage theft offence does not arise; underpaid in 2024: not answered here.
#ASSERT `Is it an offence under this Act for my employer to withhold my wages` (`d` 15 1 2026) EQUALS `repealed`
#ASSERT `Is it an offence under this Act for my employer to withhold my wages` (`d` 15 6 2024) EQUALS `in force then`
#ASSERT `Is it an offence under this Act for my employer to withhold my wages` (`d` 11 12 2025) EQUALS `in force then`
#ASSERT `Is it an offence under this Act for my employer to withhold my wages` (`d` 12 12 2025) EQUALS `repealed`
#ASSERT `Is it an offence under this Act for my employer to withhold my wages` (`d` 1 1 2021) EQUALS `not yet`
#ASSERT `Can an inspector use powers under this Act to look into my underpayment` (`d` 7 11 2026) EQUALS `repealed`
#ASSERT `Can an inspector use powers under this Act to look into my underpayment` (`d` 1 12 2025) EQUALS `in force then`

§§ `s 3 -- worker`

#ASSERT `Am I a worker` `paid` `site` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a worker` `volunteer` `residence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a worker` `contractor` `site` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a worker` `contractor` `residence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a worker` `paid` `home only` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I a worker` `paid` `no workplace` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I a worker` `no engagement` `site` EQUALS JUST FALSE

